---
title: M-Ranked — migration and cutover sequence
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor O as Operator
    participant L as Legacy FastAPI + SQLite
    participant I as Idempotent importer
    participant PG as PostgreSQL
    participant C as Target Python collectors
    participant A as Spring API
    participant N as Next.js / Nginx
    participant V as Verification suite

    Note over O,V: Gate 0: feature inventory, metric semantics, ADRs, golden dataset and rollback owner approved
    O->>PG: Apply Flyway target schema
    O->>L: Freeze legacy DDL, keep reads and collection running
    L-->>I: Online SQLite backup snapshot S0
    I->>PG: Initial load using natural keys and idempotency constraints
    I->>PG: Record migration batch, source hash and row counts
    V->>L: Read golden/current samples
    V->>PG: Compare identities, counts, NULL/zero and time series

    loop Catch-up until lag is below threshold
        I->>L: Read rows newer than last migration watermark
        I->>PG: Upsert/append incremental batch
        V->>PG: Check lag and reconciliation report
    end

    O->>A: Deploy Spring API in shadow mode
    O->>N: Deploy Next.js on non-public route
    V->>L: Execute legacy contract queries
    V->>A: Execute equivalent API queries
    V->>V: Compare normalized responses and performance budget

    Note over O,V: Cutover window begins, public legacy reads remain available
    O->>L: Stop legacy collector only
    L-->>I: Final consistent SQLite backup S-final
    I->>PG: Final catch-up transaction
    V->>PG: Validate row counts, constraints, aggregates and freshness

    alt Validation failed
        O->>L: Restart legacy collector
        O->>N: Keep legacy route
        Note over O,PG: PostgreSQL remains shadow, investigate without data loss.
    else Validation passed
        O->>C: Start target collectors against PostgreSQL
        C->>PG: First controlled collection run
        V->>PG: Verify no duplicates and revision advance
        O->>N: Switch public upstream to Next.js + Spring API
        N->>A: Production traffic
        A->>PG: Production reads
        O->>I: Start temporary PG → legacy compatibility sync

        alt SLO or correctness regression during rollback window
            O->>N: Switch upstream back to legacy web
            O->>C: Stop target collectors
            I->>L: Complete compatibility sync to rollback SQLite
            O->>L: Restart legacy collector
        else Stable through rollback window
            O->>I: Stop compatibility sync
            O->>L: Archive final SQLite and make legacy stack offline
            O->>PG: Mark migration complete
        end
    end

    Note over O,V: Never combine cutover with a new formula or changed metric semantics.
